From 9f2cc548daca81984e42f5b363d842f138935ce4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dax Raad <d@ironbay.co>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 21:23:07 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] migration: temporary Worker export and handoff endpoints for
 the move to Fly

POST /api/admin/export returns the stored TunnelObject records (and renewal alarms) for a list of Durable
Object IDs or tunnel names; POST /api/admin/handoff closes a tunnel's bridges with 1012 so clients reconnect
to the new server, and stops the Worker renewing it. Both need the ADMIN_EXPORT_TOKEN bearer secret and
answer 404 without it. Production also answers on workers.dev so the new server can reach the Worker once
opentunnel.xyz points at it. migration/worker.ts drives both for every Durable Object in the namespace.
